<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
  <title>Concept B — Orbital Megastructure</title>
  <style>
    :root{--bg:#030506;--text:#f5f7f7;--muted:#9ea9ae;--line:#243138;--ice:#d8e9ee;--blue:#173b52;font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text)}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{background:var(--bg)}body{margin:0;background:linear-gradient(#020405,#05090c 55%,#020405)}a{color:inherit}.top{position:absolute;z-index:5;top:0;left:0;width:100%;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font:700 .7rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero{min-height:100vh;position:relative;overflow:hidden;display:flex;align-items:flex-end}.stars{position:absolute;inset:0;background-image:radial-gradient(circle at 18% 22%,rgba(255,255,255,.5) 0 1px,transparent 1.5px),radial-gradient(circle at 72% 13%,rgba(255,255,255,.35) 0 1px,transparent 1.5px),radial-gradient(circle at 82% 44%,rgba(255,255,255,.2) 0 1px,transparent 1.5px),radial-gradient(circle at 31% 62%,rgba(255,255,255,.25) 0 1px,transparent 1.5px)}.earth{position:absolute;width:min(78vw,1100px);aspect-ratio:1;right:-18vw;bottom:-49vw;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle at 32% 28%,#38627c 0,#17384d 22%,#0a1720 52%,#030608 68%);box-shadow:0 -30px 100px rgba(86,159,202,.17),inset 40px 35px 90px rgba(255,255,255,.05)}.earth:after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-2px;border-radius:50%;border-top:2px solid rgba(184,226,242,.55);transform:rotate(-15deg)}.tether{position:absolute;width:2px;height:170vh;left:61%;top:-33vh;background:linear-gradient(to bottom,rgba(255,255,255,.08),#d6e1e4 18%,#fff 49%,#73838a 82%,rgba(255,255,255,.08));transform:rotate(24deg);transform-origin:center;box-shadow:0 0 13px rgba(255,255,255,.14)}.tether:before,.tether:after{content:"";position:absolute;left:50%;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#f5f8f9;transform:translateX(-50%)}.tether:before{top:6%}.tether:after{bottom:6%}.hero-copy{position:relative;z-index:3;width:min(1200px,calc(100% - 3rem));margin:0 auto;padding:8rem 0 5rem}.eyebrow{font:700 .7rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c2d6de}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(4rem,9vw,9.2rem);line-height:.84;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:.7rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:8ch}.hero p{max-width:47rem;font-size:clamp(1.12rem,2vw,1.45rem);line-height:1.52;color:#c2cbd0}.scale{position:absolute;right:2rem;top:27%;z-index:4;font:600 .68rem/1.4 ui-monospace,monospace;color:#aab8be}.scale:before{content:"";display:block;width:8rem;border-top:1px solid #aab8be;margin-bottom:.6rem}.scroll{position:absolute;left:1.5rem;bottom:1.5rem;z-index:4;font:700 .66rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#839197}.section{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 3rem));margin:auto;padding:8rem 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09)}.section .kicker{font:700 .7rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b7cdd5}.section h2{font-size:clamp(3rem,6vw,6.7rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:.7rem 0 2rem;max-width:11ch}.section .lede{font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:48rem;color:#c0c9cd}.motion{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:5rem;align-items:center;margin-top:4rem}.motion svg{width:100%;display:block}.motion p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.sequence{margin-top:4rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.seq{min-height:16rem;padding:1.3rem;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.seq span{font:700 .68rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;color:#9fb8c3}.seq h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin:3rem 0 .7rem}.seq p{font-size:.96rem;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted)}.close{min-height:75vh;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:5rem 1.5rem;position:relative;overflow:hidden}.close:before{content:"";position:absolute;width:70vw;aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:50%;bottom:-59vw;background:radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0,#163d55,#071018 48%,#010203 69%);box-shadow:0 -15px 70px rgba(93,173,214,.12)}.close div{position:relative;z-index:2}.close h2{font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,8rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.07em;max-width:12ch;margin:auto}.close p{color:var(--muted);max-width:42rem;margin:1.5rem auto}.back{position:fixed;right:1rem;bottom:1rem;z-index:9;border:1px solid #34444b;background:rgba(3,5,6,.8);padding:.75rem 1rem;text-decoration:none;font:700 .68rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}@media(max-width:800px){.motion{grid-template-columns:1fr}.sequence{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.earth{width:110vw;right:-48vw;bottom:-55vw}.tether{left:70%}.scale{display:none}}@media(max-width:520px){.sequence{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero-copy,.section{width:calc(100% - 2rem)}.top span:nth-child(2){display:none}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="back" href="/concepts/">All directions</a>
  <header class="top"><span>Skyhook Industries / Concept B</span><span>Orbital Megastructure</span></header>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="stars"></div><div class="earth"></div><div class="tether"></div>
      <div class="scale">~4,000 km STUDY LENGTH</div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A rotating transportation system in orbit</p>
        <h1>Catch the payload. Swing it higher.</h1>
        <p>A Skyhook is a tether thousands of kilometres long, rotating freely around Earth. At the bottom of each rotation, its lower tip can meet a vehicle arriving from the atmosphere. The tether takes the payload, carries it upward, and releases it with more orbital energy than the vehicle could have reached alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scroll">Scroll / follow the tether</div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="kicker">The machine</p><h2>Two motions. One rendezvous.</h2><p class="lede">The whole structure circles Earth while the tether turns around its own center of mass. At the bottom of the rotation, those velocities partially cancel. For a few seconds, the lower tip becomes something a vehicle from Earth can plausibly chase.</p>
      <div class="motion">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 480" role="img" aria-label="Diagram showing orbital and rotational motion">
          <defs><marker id="ab" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="#d8e9ee"/></marker></defs>
          <circle cx="280" cy="390" r="165" fill="#0b1a23" stroke="#284554"/>
          <ellipse cx="280" cy="247" rx="218" ry="88" fill="none" stroke="#3a4a51" stroke-dasharray="6 8"/>
          <g transform="rotate(-28 282 207)"><line x1="150" y1="337" x2="434" y2="73" stroke="#e9f1f3" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="282" cy="207" r="8" fill="#f5f7f7"/><circle cx="150" cy="337" r="6" fill="#cfe0e5"/></g>
          <path d="M130 323 C95 310 79 286 68 260" fill="none" stroke="#d8e9ee" marker-end="url(#ab)"/>
          <path d="M387 116 C418 102 441 83 454 57" fill="none" stroke="#d8e9ee" marker-end="url(#ab)"/>
          <text x="42" y="242" fill="#9dafb6" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">LOWER TIP</text><text x="391" y="44" fill="#9dafb6" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">ROTATION</text><text x="296" y="199" fill="#9dafb6" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">COM</text>
        </svg>
        <div><p>The lower tip is not hovering. It is still moving at hypersonic speed relative to Earth. The trick is to make it move <em>far less quickly than an ordinary object in the same orbit</em> at exactly the moment the vehicle arrives.</p><p>That is the heart of the system: put a reusable orbital structure where a rocket stage would normally be doing the work.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="kicker">One pass</p><h2>A few minutes that change the payload’s orbit.</h2>
      <div class="sequence"><article class="seq"><span>01 / CLIMB</span><h3>Approach</h3><p>The vehicle climbs onto a precisely timed intercept trajectory.</p></article><article class="seq"><span>02 / CONTACT</span><h3>Capture</h3><p>The lower tip takes the payload and transfers the load into the tether.</p></article><article class="seq"><span>03 / ROTATION</span><h3>Swing</h3><p>The payload rides the tether upward and gains orbital energy.</p></article><article class="seq"><span>04 / DEPARTURE</span><h3>Release</h3><p>The payload leaves on a higher-energy trajectory. The tether begins rebuilding the momentum it gave away.</p></article></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="kicker">Design language</p><h2>The page should feel as large as the machine.</h2><p class="lede">This direction makes the tether the composition rather than an illustration inside the composition. Scale, Earth curvature and motion do the emotional work. Technical diagrams arrive only after the reader understands the physical idea.</p><p class="lede">For a final site, this is the strongest homepage language. It needs the discipline of Concept A underneath it so the spectacle always resolves into evidence and engineering.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="close"><div><h2>Orbital infrastructure should not have to be thrown away after every flight.</h2><p>The Skyhook proposal is an attempt to turn part of the launch problem into a machine that stays in orbit and gets used again.</p></div></section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
